From: Starch Linux project
Subject: [PATCH] build: use the packaged pybind11 headers

The bundled pybind11 2.11.1 predates Python 3.14. Arch's packaged pybind11
tracks the Python toolchain and is used only while compiling the bindings.

---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 132b4741..780abcf2 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -651,7 +651,7 @@ set(Calamares_LIBRARIES calamares)
 
 add_subdirectory(3rdparty/kdsingleapplication)
 if(WITH_PYBIND11)
-    add_subdirectory(3rdparty/pybind11)
+    find_package(pybind11 CONFIG REQUIRED)
 endif()
 add_subdirectory(src)
 
